  "titleRes": "how_to_play_step4_title",
  "bodyRes": "how_to_play_step4_body",
  "body": "Driving over an oil spill takes away your steering for the next turn. The coast is always available, plus two randomly chosen nearby points — your choices are restricted. Slow down before a spill, or steer around it.",
  "notes": "Six-frame walkthrough of an oil spill, following GameEngine.oilSlipTargets: a move whose path touches the spill costs the player their steering on the *next* move, when only the coast point and two randomly drawn neighbours of it are offered.\n\nThe restricted set is centred on the coast point (position + lastVelocity), not on the car — centring it on the car would show moves the engine never offers.",
